# Study of STC89C52 Microcontroller CPU and Architecture
STC89C52 Microcontroller is a 8-bit microcontroller, it is also 8051 arhitecture. The electronic unit is embedded CPU, memory, registers, GPIO ports, counters, interrupts, timers to control the electronic instruments.
Architecture of CPU
It is the main thing in the CPU, Iit takes in instructions, it decodes them and it runs them. It consists of ALU, Control Unit, registers, Stack Pointer, Program Counter and Program Status Word
Registers
Registers are storage locations within which hold data. The registers are the following: A/Accumulator, B, R0-R7, PC, SP and PSW. The register A is 8 bits, and is employed in arithmetic, logic and data transfer instructions. The B register is used in arithmetic operations. R0-R7). They are general purpose 8bit registers.
Program Counter and Stack Pointer_
PC is a 16-bit register that holds the address of next instruction. SP is an 8 bit register that points to the top of the stack. One uses LIFO, for the stack.
PSW and Memory
The PSW is the register that contains the status and control information of the CPU, including flags for Carry, Auxiliary Carry, Overflow, Parity as well as the register-bank selection flags. In program memory the instructions are stored, and in data memory the information needed during execution is stored.
GPIO, Timers and Interrupts
STC89C52 has four 8-bit ports, P0, P1, P2, and P3. They interface with outside world . Timer 0 and Timer 1 can be programmed to work as the timer or the counter. Interrupts allow the CPU to be responsive to significant events which are executed as Interrupt Service Routine thereby temporarily halting the main program.
Overall Working..
The CPU continuously fetches, decodes and executes the instruction. Registers, memory,gpio,timers, stack, interrupts and so on collaborately do work. 
